<table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b>''Madonna's Drowned Worlds'': New Book Out in April.</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=22"><img src="images/topics/book.gif" border="0" Alt="Books" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><SPAN class=postbody><STRONG>"Madonna’s Drowned Worlds: New Approaches to Her Cultural Transformations (1983-2003)"</STRONG> [<SPAN class=postbody><STRONG>Santiago Fouz-Hernández</STRONG> and <STRONG>Freya Jarman-Ivans</STRONG>, editors (<STRONG>Ashgate</STRONG>, 2004) ISBN 0754633713 and 0754633721] will be</SPAN></SPAN><SPAN class=postbody>&nbsp;out in April 2004. Read every details:</SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody></SPAN><SPAN class=postbody><BR>CONTEXT AND RATIONALE <BR>In the ten years since the publication of <STRONG>The Madonna Connection</STRONG> - the most recent major collection of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> essays in <STRONG>English</STRONG> - <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>, perhaps one of the most consistently transgressive and self-transforming artists of the late 20th and early 21st century, has presented a set of strikingly new challenges to cultural analysis. <BR><BR>The release of <STRONG>Evita</STRONG> in 1996 was at once the culmination of her recurrent interest in Hispanism and the beginning of an unexpected transformation into exemplary matriarch. The arrival of her two children, her second marriage, the release of two critically acclaimed and best-selling albums and a sold-out world tour (her first tour in eight years), have renewed media interest in her. This new attention seems to have been attracted in no small part by the latest transformations, which seem, on the surface at least, to signal a dislocation with past personae. This putative dislocation generates a new set of resources which includes two films, several new songs and music videos, and also various media interviews and public statements worthy of academic study. New developments in <STRONG>Gender</STRONG>, <STRONG>Queer and Ethnic</STRONG> studies also shed new light on her entire oeuvre. <BR><BR>In view of this, the present volume aims to offer new perspectives on <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s work to date, (re)addressing her configurations of race, gender and sex(uality) and with special emphasis on her resurrection after the Sex backlash in the early 1990s. Hence, our contributions focus on new <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>-related topics such as Hinduism, Judaism, Japanese culture (the Geisha look), All-American culture, Queer culture, Motherhood and her influence on newer 'girl acts' such as the <STRONG>Spice Girls</STRONG> or <STRONG>Britney Spears</STRONG>. While our contributors refer to classic cultural theorists, such as <STRONG>Baudrillard</STRONG>, <STRONG>Zizek</STRONG>, <STRONG>Foucault</STRONG> or <STRONG>Barthes</STRONG>, the book also features new theoretical approaches to <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s work. Such new approaches include the fusion of classical music studies with popular musicology (<STRONG>Clifton</STRONG>), a reading of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s videos from an alchemical and hermeticist perspective (<STRONG>Herr</STRONG>) or an investigation of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s commercial appeal as a celebrity in the context of global economy (<STRONG>Peñaloza</STRONG>). <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s recent engagement with All-American culture has provided an interesting new perspective on her relationship with ethnic identities, as shown in one of our essays (<STRONG>Albiez</STRONG>).</SPAN> </P>
<P><STRONG><EM>Read more...</EM></STRONG></P><br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Thanks to <STRONG>HolidayGuy</STRONG></SPAN>. Published at 6:25pm W. Europe 
Standard Time. </i>

</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


