<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><STRONG>Valentine's Day</STRONG> probably features the second-highest number of compilation and theme album has released, after the <STRONG>Christmas</STRONG> season. <BR><BR>This year, <STRONG>Hear Music</STRONG> releases a collection called <STRONG>"Sweetheart: Love Songs,"</STRONG> which features some of the most interesting musicians around - including <STRONG>Aimee Mann</STRONG>, <STRONG>Clem Snide</STRONG>, <STRONG>Kathleen Edwards</STRONG>, <STRONG>Nada Surf</STRONG>, <STRONG><U>Joe Henry</U></STRONG> and <STRONG>Ron Sexsmith</STRONG> - covering their favorite love songs.<BR><BR><STRONG>Miho Hatori</STRONG> radically reworked <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s <STRONG>"Crazy for You"</STRONG> into a jazzy number with subtly dissonant horns.<BR><BR><STRONG>"Sweetheart"</STRONG> comes with first-rate liner notes, in which each artist explains his or her choice. <br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Read it first here: Published at 12:40am W. Europe Standard Time. Source: 
<STRONG>CtNow</STRONG>.</i>

</font></div>
