<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=8"><img src="images/topics/interviste.gif" border="0" Alt="Interviews" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P class=articleheadtypea align=left>Speaking at the 30th birthday party in <STRONG>London</STRONG> of <STRONG>Supergrass</STRONG> drummer <STRONG>Danny Goffey</STRONG>, <STRONG>Samantha Morton</STRONG>, star of TV hit Soldier Soldier, criticised <STRONG>Liz Hurley</STRONG> and <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>.</P>
<P class=articleheadtypea align=left>Asked how she landed her role in <STRONG>"Sweet And Lowdown,"</STRONG> she explained: '<STRONG>Woody</STRONG> really loves film. As a filmmaker he wants to soak up everything new, not in the way <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> is good at seeing what's happening and then snatching it and stealing it, reinventing herself in that way.'</P><br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Read it first here: Published at 11:53am W. Europe Standard Time. Source: <STRONG>The Mirror</STRONG> and <STRONG>Evening Standard</STRONG>.&nbsp; </i>

</font></div>
