<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=21"><img src="images/topics/web.gif" border="0" Alt="Web" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><STRONG><A href="http://www.audible.com" target=_blank>Audible</A></STRONG>, the leading provider of digitally delivered spoken word audio, today announced financial results for the quarter and year ended December 31, 2003. Their sales have grown. "Our growth rate for the fourth quarter of 2003 and the milestone achievement of positive free cash flow ahead of our expectations testify to the fundamental power of <A href="http://www.audible.com/" target=_blank><STRONG>Audible</STRONG></A>'s business model," said <STRONG>Donald Katz</STRONG>, Chairman and CEO, <A href="http://www.audible.com/" target=_blank><STRONG>Audible</STRONG></A>. <BR>On a press release, they mention their partnership initiatives with <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> and <STRONG>Penguin</STRONG> as one of their recent highlights. <br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Read it first here: Published at 0:10am W. Europe Standard Time. Source: <STRONG>Business Wire</STRONG>. </i>

</font></div>
