<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=16"><img src="images/topics/charts.gif" border="0" Alt="Charts" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><OL>
<LI>Britney Spears, 2000 MTV Video Music Awards</LI>
<LI><STRONG>Madonna Performs "Like a Virgin," 1984 MTV Video Music Awards<BR>HOT BECAUSE: La Ciccone's wedding dress-clad performance of "Like a Virgin" was so ahead-of-the-curve provocative that 19 years later, Britney and Christina revived it at the VMAs prior to getting kissy-kissy with the Material Girl herself. But Madonna's performance at MTV's inaugural awards bash remains definitively raunchy, as she prowled the stage and grabbed her crotch in a manner summed up by Melissa Etheridge as "the most brave, blatant sexual thing I've ever seen on television."</STRONG></LI>
<LI>Elvis Presley, The Ed Sullivan Show, 1956</LI>
<LI>Chris Isaak, "Wicked Game" Video, 1991</LI>
<LI>Baywatch Opening Credits, 1989-2001</LI>
<LI>Britney Spears, "...Baby One More Time" Video, 1998</LI>
<LI>Jennifer Lopez's Green Dress, 2000 Grammy Awards</LI>
<LI>James Brown, The T.A.M.I. Show, 1964</LI>
<LI>Friends, "The One Where Ross and Rachel... You Know" Episode, 1996</LI>
<LI><STRONG>Madonna on "Wayne's World," Saturday Night Live, 1991<BR>HOT BECAUSE: The sketch spoofed Madonna's black-and-white "Justify My Love" video, famously banned from MTV in 1990 for "explicit sexuality"- which means you're not sure whether to laugh or drool. Wayne and Garth fantasize about playing Truth or Dare with "the number 1 hot babe of all time," and the dream culminates in a lipstick-smeared make-out session in which Madonna spills out of a black bustier and writhes on a heap of pillows. Excellent, indeed.<BR>NOT BECAUSE: The sight of Dana Carvey's catsuit bulge almost cancels out Madonna's lingerie.</STRONG></LI>
<LI>"Ann Margrock," The Flintstones, 1963</LI>
<LI>Christina Aguilera, "Dirrty" Video, 2002</LI>
<LI>George Michael, 'Freedom' 90" Video, 1990</LI>
<LI>Happy Days, "Fonzie: Rock Entrepreneur" Episode, November 1977</LI>
<LI>Jennifer Lopez, "Jenny From the Block" Video, 2002</LI>
<LI>Duran Duran, "Girls on Film (Long Uncensored Version)" Video, 1982</LI>
<LI>Fiona Apple, "Criminal" Video, 1996</LI>
<LI>D'Angelo, "Untitled (How Does It Feel?") Video, 2000</LI>
<LI>Enrique Iglesias, "Addicted" Video, 2003</LI>
<LI>The Simpsons, "Colonel Homer" Episode, 1992</LI>
<LI>Rose McGowan's Mesh Dress, 1998 MTV Video Music Awards</LI>
<LI>The Rolling Stones Perform "Let's Spend the Night Together," The Ed Sullivan Show, 1967</LI>
<LI><STRONG>Madonna, Britney and Christina Lip-Lock 2003 MTV Video Music Awards<BR>HOT BECAUSE: Actually, according to Britney Spears, her appearance was not that hot. "I don't understand what the big deal is," she claimed. "Hasn't America ever seen two girls kiss before?" Well, possibly. But what the country hadn't seen was two- scratch that, <I>three</I>- female megastars getting it on lipstick lesbian-style, as Madonna first removed garters from Spears and Christina Aguilera before kissing them both. But it could have been hotter! "I was up for kissing Britney," Aguilera told Blender. "But Britney wasn't."<BR>NOT BECAUSE: Instead of the Madonna Aguilera smooch, some genius at MTV decided instead to show a reaction shot from Justin Timberlake. D'oh!</STRONG></LI>
<LI>T.A.T.U., 2003 MTV Movie Awards</LI>
<LI>Fountains of Wayne, "Stacy's Mom" video</LI></OL><br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Special thanks to <STRONG>HolidayGuy</STRONG>.</i>

</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


