<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=31"><img src="images/topics/nonsolomadonnna.gif" border="0" Alt="Non Solo Madonna" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><STRONG>"The Ten Commandments: The Spectacle Musical"</STRONG> will open in September at the <STRONG>Kodak Theater</STRONG>, home of the <STRONG>Oscars</STRONG>, on <STRONG>Hollywood Boulevard</STRONG>.</P>
<P>The biblical <SPAN class=infused><SPAN class=infusedKeyword>tuner</SPAN><ABBR></SPAN> has parted curtains before. It previously toured <STRONG>Belgium</STRONG>, <STRONG>Switzerland</STRONG> and <STRONG>France</STRONG>, where it played the 4,000-seat <STRONG>Palais des Sports</STRONG> in <STRONG>Paris</STRONG> for six months in 2003.</P>
<P>The U.S. version would be an entirely new production with a new score by lyricist <STRONG>Meribeth Derry</STRONG> (<STRONG>"Fame L.A."</STRONG>) and composer <STRONG>Patrick Leonard</STRONG>, who wrote and produced so many songs with <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>.&nbsp;<STRONG>Pascal Obispo</STRONG> wrote the European score.</P>
<P>An American choreographer would be announced shortly. </P>
<P>There will be a cast of 50 dancers and singers.</P>
<P>After the open-ended <STRONG>Los Angeles</STRONG> engagement, <STRONG>"The Ten Commandments"</STRONG> looks to a 17-month national tour.</P><br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Read it first here: Published at 2:34am W. Europe Standard Time. Source: 
<STRONG>The Variety</STRONG>.</i>

</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


