<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000">When <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> arrived at the <STRONG>Grammy Awards 2004</STRONG>, walking th red carpet, she was asked to comment on the controversial <STRONG>Janet Jackson</STRONG> and <STRONG>Justin Timberlake</STRONG> 's perfomance at the <STRONG>Super Bowl</STRONG>. She replied rolling up her eyes. And, relying on <STRONG>"Entertainment Tonight,"</STRONG> she said (in a really English accent tone) "No, I have no opinion about it, much to do about nothing." <BR>Then, <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> rightly stated (at <STRONG>"Access Hollywod"</STRONG>) that "In this country people react over the silliest things", so she's not surprised about the reaction. <BR>Finally, <STRONG>"Entertainment Tonight"</STRONG> asked what award she's there to present and she ironically responded, "I'm here to kiss <STRONG>Janet Jackson</STRONG>." <br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Info: <STRONG>Peppermint</STRONG> and <STRONG>Slyguy</STRONG>. Published at 1:38am W. Europe Standard Time. </i>

